/// AgentBackend — Protocol for coding-agent backends driven by AgentRunner.
///
/// Any backend that can open a session, run turns from prompts, and stream
/// events structurally conforms (no explicit adoption needed; pinned by
/// `conformsTo:` unit tests). CodexClient and ClaudeBackend both
/// implement it. AgentRunner holds the backend as
/// `CodexClient | ClaudeBackend` — a protocol-typed field rejects both
/// today, so the union carries the seam until the checker accepts
/// declared conformance — and picks the concrete class from config.
///
/// Seam contract (mirrors the CodexClient shapes the runner was built on):
/// - `startSession` opens the backend and answers `{"threadId" => id}`
///   (the backend's session handle under one key). A backend whose
///   handle only exists after the first turn (Claude's init arrives
///   post-prompt) may answer "" and publish the real id via init
///   events instead.
/// - `startTurn:sessionId:prompt:title:` sends one prompt and answers
///   turn metadata (title is advisory; backends may ignore it).
/// - `streamStep` reads the next event: nil means no terminal event yet
///   (call again); a Result ends the turn.
/// - `stopProcess` shuts the backend down; safe to call twice.
Protocol define: AgentBackend
  startSession -> Result(Dictionary, TaggedError)
  startTurn: sessionId :: String prompt: prompt :: String title: title :: String -> Result(Dictionary, TaggedError)
  streamStep -> Result(Dictionary, TaggedError) | Nil
  turnTimeout -> TaggedError
  stopProcess -> Nil
